Since $T$ is a linear transformation, we have that

$$
\begin{aligned}T(v+kw)=T(v)+T(kw)=T(v)+kT(w)\end{aligned}
$$

for any vectors $v$ and $w.$ Therefore,

$$
\begin{aligned}T({v}_{1}+2{v}_{2}) & =T({v}_{1})+2T({v}_{2}) \\ [\begin{aligned}14 \\ 10\end{aligned}] & =[\begin{aligned}6 \\ 2\end{aligned}]+2T({v}_{2}) \\ 2T({v}_{2}) & =[\begin{aligned}14 \\ 10\end{aligned}]-[\begin{aligned}6 \\ 2\end{aligned}] \\ 2T({v}_{2}) & =[\begin{aligned}8 \\ 8\end{aligned}] \\ T({v}_{2}) & =\frac{1}{2}[\begin{aligned}8 \\ 8\end{aligned}] \\ T({v}_{2}) & =[\begin{aligned}4 \\ 4\end{aligned}].\end{aligned}
$$

